CCOOMMPPAATTIIBBIILLIITTYY
     hhoosstt aims to be reasonably compatible with ‘host’ utility from BIND9 dis‐
     tribution, both in supported options and in produced output.  Here is a
     list of known notable differences:

     ••   Debugging options (--DD and --mm) are not supported.

     ••   Query class CCLLAASSSS00 and type TTYYPPEE00 are not supported.

     ••   Backslashes in domain names are treated especially.

     ••   The maximum of 255 retries (option --RR) are supported.

     ••   Some resource records are formatted differently.  For example, RRRRSSIIGG
         and DDNNSSKKEEYY records are displayed without spaces in them.

     ••   When parsing _/_e_t_c_/_r_e_s_o_l_v_._c_o_n_f commands ssoorrttlliisstt and ooppttiioonnss are ig‐
         nored.  When multiple sseeaarrcchh and/or ddoommaaiinn commands are present, hhoosstt
         first uses the last ddoommaaiinn command, and then all of sseeaarrcchh commands,
         while ‘host’ from BIND9 uses whatever command was specified last.

     ••   ‘Pseudosection TSIG’ is missing from verbose packet output.

